From 78c2c4314be4f93c375d5b425b349c543017dd54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:21:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?tor41339:=20item=204=20on=20.7=20=E2=80=94=20re?=
 =?UTF-8?q?fuse=20BEGIN=5FDIR=20before=20alloc=20without=20losing=20counts?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Rework of the cleanup-indexing item 4 (refuse an over-limit BEGIN_DIR before
edge_connection_new()) for the +tor41339.7 series, which instruments the
BEGIN_DIR path. A mechanical move of the old post-allocation
dos_should_refuse_begindir() block would silently drop two new counts; this
keeps both, per the Directory-flood metrics agent's note:

- dos_should_refuse_begindir() returns the over-max result through a
  bool out-parameter instead of marking the stream (there is no stream yet
  before allocation); connection_exit_begin_conn() applies it to n_stream
  after allocation, so connection_exit_connect_dir() still copies
  begindir_over_max onto the directory connection and the over-max requests
  family still counts served-but-over-max streams.
- dos_note_begindir_stream_rate() is pulled out of dos_should_refuse_begindir()
  and called from connection_exit_begin_conn() after the hibernation check,
  so begindir_over_stream_rate still counts only after the directory and
  hibernation checks (its commit's contract), not before them.
- The pre-allocation refuse is skipped while hibernating, so the hibernation
  refusal keeps precedence (END_STREAM_REASON_HIBERNATING) and the counts are
  byte-for-byte the .7 counts in that case.

Enforcement is off in the deployment, so in production (count-only) the counts
are identical to .7; the only divergence is that an over-limit-AND-enforced
refused cell is no longer also counted toward begindir_over_stream_rate, which
is more correct (it was refused for a different reason) and dormant while the
limit is off. Updates the 0020/0024 unit tests for the new signature and the
standalone rate-count call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
